# Domain and Database

The canonical transcript is timestamped segments, not one giant string. VTT is an export artifact.

```ts
export interface TranscriptSegment {
  id: string;
  sequence: number;
  startMs: number;
  endMs: number;
  speaker?: string;
  text: string;
}
```

## Recordings

Statuses: `uploaded` | `processing` | `ready` | `failed`.

Postgres (Drizzle in `packages/db`) stores metadata and object keys, never video binaries or embeddings.

## Knowledge bases

Scopes: `recording` (one KB per recording) and `global` (one project-wide KB).

Store `provider` and `provider_knowledge_base_id`. “Add to global KB” goes through `KnowledgeBaseProvider` — do not copy vectors into PostgreSQL.

## Domain package

`packages/domain` holds product types and rules (`recordings`, `transcripts`, `summaries`, `hooks`, `clips`, `knowledge`, `jobs`). It must not import providers or vendor SDKs.
